  "interpretation": "At small N pandas wins because Dask pays a fixed graph-build + shuffle overhead the in-memory pandas path does not. The crossover appears as N grows and the per-card groupby/merge can be parallelised across cores. Both backends produce identical feature matrices (max_abs_diff <= 1e-6), so Dask is a drop-in replacement for the single-node pandas engineer as data volume grows."
